#
# First bindeb-pkg attempt failed under -j32 at the AR step for
# rust/built-in.a: `ar: rust/bindings.o: No such file or directory`. The log
# shows `RUSTC L rust/bindings.o` firing TWICE (two separate make jobs both
# decided to rebuild it), and the object was gone by the time ar needed it , a
# parallel-build race in Kbuild's rust/ dependency graph, not a patch defect
# (none of the 24 patches touch anything under rust/). Fix: no `make clean`,
# just re-invoke the same `bindeb-pkg` build , Kbuild is incremental and only
# rebuilds what's missing, and the retry completed clean. If a future 7.2.1
# rebuild hits the identical `ar: rust/bindings.o` failure, retry before
# re-diagnosing the patches.
#
# Read patches/kernel-org-7.1/series as well — its long runtime-verification
