# 0023 — NOT ours. cache_ext (Tal Zussman et al., SOSP '25,
# https://doi.org/10.1145/3731569.3764820, GPL-2.0), forward-ported from
# their v6.6.8 fork. Track B carry: their authorship stays, we add no
# Signed-off-by. Inert until a BPF program is loaded and its cgroup enabled
# via /proc/page_cache_ext_enabled_cgroup.
#
# Its 7.1.10 history is the reason to re-check it hard on every bump: the
# first forward-port compiled clean and failed at initcall, because it
# carried 6.6.8's BTF_SET8_START (flags 0) where 7.1 wants BTF_KFUNCS_START
# (flags BTF_SET8_KFUNCS). All eight kfuncs were missing from the verifier's
# table while the struct_ops half registered happily, so it looked fine from
# userspace. Fixed, and confirmed clean on the 2026-08-27 boot — no
# btf.c:9004 WARNING, /proc/page_cache_ext_enabled_cgroup present.
#
# STILL UNPROVEN, on 7.1.10 and here: whether its call sites in mm/filemap.c
# and mm/vmscan.c actually fire. A registered struct_ops whose hooks never
# run is indistinguishable from a working one. Do not treat a clean `git am`
# on 7.2 as evidence either way.
